          "text": "'Death by Astonishment: Confronting the Mystery of the World's Strangest Drug' now available in the UK and Europe wherever books are sold...\n\n\"A long overdue and brilliant piece of work with nods to many classics: the turn of phrase of McKenna, the anthropological scope of Narby, the historical depth of Mike Jay, the raw and in your faceness of Burroughs, and a hint of Lovecraftian & Poe horror… I think this is somewhat of a masterpiece.\"\n\n-- Dr. David Luke\n\nThank you @drdluke!\n\n\"In a story that begins in the Amazonian rainforests and ends somewhere beyond the stars, the first detailed account of the discovery of DMT and science’s continuing struggle to explain how such a simple and common plant molecule can have such astonishing effects on the human mind...\"\n\n(Inside cover art by Harry Pack and INCEDIGRIS)"
